{
  "an3.62:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.62 ",
  "an3.62:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an3.62:0.3": "Perils ",
  "an3.62:1.1": "“Mendicants, an unlearned ordinary person speaks of three perils that tear mothers and children apart. ",
  "an3.62:1.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.62:1.3": "There comes a time when a great fire flares up, ",
  "an3.62:1.4": "and it burns villages, towns, and cities. ",
  "an3.62:1.5": "When this happens, a mother can’t find her child, and a child can’t find their mother. ",
  "an3.62:1.6": "This is the first peril that tears mothers and children apart. ",
  "an3.62:2.1": "Furthermore, there comes a time when a great storm gathers, ",
  "an3.62:2.2": "and it unleashes a mighty flood ",
  "an3.62:2.3": "that sweeps away villages, towns, and cities. ",
  "an3.62:2.4": "When this happens, a mother can’t find her child, and a child can’t find their mother. ",
  "an3.62:2.5": "This is the second peril that tears mothers and children apart. ",
  "an3.62:3.1": "Furthermore, there comes a time of peril due to turmoil in the wilds, so the countryfolk mount their vehicles and flee everywhere. ",
  "an3.62:3.2": "When this happens, a mother can’t find her child, and a child can’t find their mother. ",
  "an3.62:3.3": "This is the third peril that tears mothers and children apart. ",
  "an3.62:3.4": "These are the three perils an unlearned ordinary person speaks of that tear mothers and children apart. ",
  "an3.62:4.1": "Mendicants, an unlearned ordinary person speaks of three peri